{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1790331494,"nonce":"H3BY3cU49agKERnKYZp5iiujoFQ=","target":"4da50c2330f661bf0adf4f6e015567d3cb5c60e60ee3672657b9bc42819ad7e7","message":"`crates/zyntax_lua/conformance/official/` carries the test suite that ships with Lua 5.4.9 (lua.org/tests), run per file with `_U=true` as `all.lua` runs it. Two files pass because they bail out on a missing `T` (code.lua, tracegc.lua); the other 26 stop early. What stops each, first blocker first:\n\n- `_G` as a value (`next(_G)`, `pairs(_G)`, `load(..., _G)`, `setmetatable(_G, ...)`): globals are module variables, and only the `_G.name`, `_G[\"name\"]`, `rawget(_G, \"name\")` and `rawset(_G, \"name\", v)` spellings are compiled, as reads and writes of the global. A real `_G` needs globals kept in a table, or a table view over the module variables.\n- `load`, `require`, `dofile`, `debug.*`, `collectgarbage`, `string.dump`: no compile-at-runtime, no module loading, no debug library.\n- `goto` other than a `goto continue` to a label ending the enclosing loop body (goto.lua, math.lua).\n- `\u003cclose\u003e` variables (cstack.lua, files.lua).\n- `pcall` / `error` with values, `xpcall`, error positions (`file:line:`): errors end the program.\n- Lua patterns: `string.find` with a pattern, `match`, `gmatch`, `gsub` (pm.lua and most others).\n- Strings are bytes in Lua: a source file that is not UTF-8 (strings.lua), `\\u{7FFFFFFF}` escapes (utf8.lua), `\\xff` in literals.\n- `string.pack`/`unpack`, `utf8.*`, `os.*` beyond clock/time/exit, `io.*` beyond write.\n\nEach of these is a feature of its own; split it out when it starts, and remove its files from KNOWN_FAILURES as they pass.","files":null}]}